  "features": [
    "POSIX polling and socket loop lifecycle implementations compile from Home; external objects are excluded. Both implementations and two loop/poll ABI headers match the Bun pin.",
    "Selected native compiler flags and header roots are retained, with explicit C language selection, byte-identical ABI checks and cache inputs.",
    "Pinned connect-error and half-open polling behavior is restored in formerly stale reference mirrors. Ordinary FIN/half-open writes and closure pass."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This ownership batch prepares the kernel-wait boundary but does not implement event-loop utilization or startup counters. Those placeholders remain open under #869.",
    "The platform selection correction is tested on Darwin arm64; Windows/libuv ownership, Linux behavioral execution, Release/ASAN and all-platform verification remain open.",
    "Disk admission refused an intermediate run; obsolete task executables were removed after all prior processes completed, and the final build/tests pass with guards unchanged.",
    "The previous ICU contradiction #872, other native dependency ownership, complete Bun suite and wider API semantics remain open under #66."
  ],
